FujiNet Go Arcadia 2001 desktop -- milestone log and what is left

Status: v0.1.0 in progress. The core (core/arc/) is done and verified against
MAME; the session, debugger and frontends are other work packages (see below).

DONE (core)
  [x] M0  skeleton cloned from the Odyssey 2 desktop (v0.1.1); firmware pin =
          PR #2259's head c38e8b446 (the real CONFIG baked into
          pico/arcadia/firmware/baked/fujiconfigrom.h), fork branch
          tschak909/fujinet-firmware arcadia-bake-config; runtime build script
          (tools/fujinet/: the patch anchors audited against the pin -- all
          found; BoIP 11522, web UI 11523)
  [x] M1  Signetics 2650 (s2650.c) + disassembler (dasm2650.c): traces
          identical to MAME on generated probes (tools/ab/s2650_ab.py)
  [x] M2  2637 UVI (uvi.c): per-line drawing from MAME's arcadia_v.cpp, the glyph
          table, UDCs, objects, collisions, pots, keypad/panel registers, the
          debugger's snapshot and renderers; beeper (sound.c)
  [x] M3  machine (machine.c): memory map, SENSE = vblank, the 262 * 60 Hz line
          timer with MAME's scheduler arithmetic, keypads/panel/fire wire, pots
          (digital ends or analog disc), RESET, PAL row (312 lines, 50 Hz; not
          verifiable against MAME, which runs every clone at NTSC)
  [x] M4  cart slot (carts.c: standard 4K/8K, Golf by CRC) and the FujiNet
          cartridge device (fujinet_cart.c: arcmap_decode connector decode,
          APPBANK window + $2D80+n select, cart RAM, 60 Hz tick $2C0E/F, swap
          at $2DFE, reconnect, trace tap) over the firmware's own fujimail /
          fujibus / arcmap / arcapp staged verbatim; host.c (paced thread)
  [x] M5  whole-machine A/B against MAME, frame for frame from frame 0:
          all 48 cartridges, 900 frames with a scripted input session; 13
          UVI stress probes (tools/ab/uvi_probes.py); CONFIG hashes
          (config_frames, no ROM needed); CONFIG on a live fujinet-pc over BoIP
          boots a game (swap at $2DFE with the mailbox on its worker thread)
  [ ] M6  session, debugger, frontends, icons, docs: other work packages

FRONTEND STATE
  KDE      built and run offscreen; QRhi GPU path and real-display behaviour
           of the fixed-size Controllers dialog unverified
  Windows  cross-built, run under Wine on a private Xvnc display; file dialogs,
           gamepads, audio, live FujiNet link and real D3D timing unverified
  GNOME    see the git log
  macOS    written against a Cocoa stub; first compile is on the GitHub runners

KNOWN GAPS / NEXT
  [ ] Palladium (16-key keypads, $1903/$1907 extra column) is not supported:
      MAME marks it not working. Golf's second 2K at $4000 (the Palladium
      layout) is mapped, as MAME's softlist does, but nothing runs it.
  [ ] MAME's pots are digital and are not gated to the vertical blank; real
      hardware reads $FF outside it. We follow MAME.
  [ ] The PAL machine row is MAME-unverifiable (MAME runs every clone at NTSC
      timing); its 312 lines / 50 Hz / 4.433619 MHz / 5 follow the driver's
      comment.
  [ ] The beeper is MAME's at 15625 Hz box-averaged to 48 kHz; no recording
      comparison was made.
  [ ] config_boot and netboot (tests/): the in-process FujiNet driving CONFIG
      and the firmware's fujiboot/fujitest clients are written against the
      session API and need the session/debugger packages to build; run them once
      those land (netboot needs ARC_TESTROM_DIR, see its header)
  [ ] MAME's input ports take a value set from a Lua frame notifier one frame
      late; tools/ab/cart_ab.py shifts its events to match, so a key pressed at
      "frame f" is held from our frame f
  [ ] fujinet-ads family banner (16 systems) and sibling README port tables
  [ ] when firmware PR #2259 merges: re-pin master, flatpak manifests back to
      `type: git`; the fork branch must not be deleted before that
